The free radicals and toxic byproducts produced by cells are scavenged by antioxidants. For this task, there is a network of antioxidant enzymes such as glutathione, superoxide dismutase, catalase and thioredoxin [1]. Glutathione is an essential antioxidant in maintaining redox balance and also in enhancing cellular antioxidant defenses [1][2].
